# RULE: Core Platform

Mandatory. Full detail: `docs/softphone/Architecture-Constitution.md`, `Engineering-Principles.md`, `STATUS.md`.

## Mission

Telephony platform — not a generic Electron app. Optimize: reliability, maintainability, replaceability, observability, testability.

## Layers (deps inward only)

```txt
UI → Application → Domain → Ports → Adapters → Infrastructure
```

## Before code

1. Feature Registry entry (`docs/softphone/Feature-Registry.md`)
2. Bounded context: Telephony | Operator | Media | Headset | Settings | Integration
3. Layer (renderer: read `docs/softphone/UI-Architecture.md`)
4. Existing abstractions, I/O, side effects, required tests
5. LF-XXX if legacy-affected (`Legacy-Feature-Coverage.md`)

Mapping: business logic→Domain; orchestration→Application; external tech→Adapters/Infrastructure; presentation→UI; contracts→Ports.

## Never

- UI→SIP/Electron/repository/filesystem/WebSocket/adapter
- Domain→React/Electron/JsSIP/Zustand/browser/Node/storage/infrastructure
- Store→Use Cases/adapters/SIP/Electron/repositories/orchestration
- Adapter→UI; JsSIP or raw SIP sessions in React or Domain
- Business rules in React, stores, or adapters
- Boolean flags as primary call state — use: Idle, Ringing, Connecting, Active, Held, Transferring, Conference, Ending, Ended, Failed
- `any`, `@ts-ignore`, `as unknown as`
- State change without Domain Event

## Always

- Business ops via Use Cases (`MakeCallUseCase`, `AnswerCallUseCase`, etc.); telephony via Call Engine
- Stores = projections only; hooks compose selectors/Use Cases/UI behavior
- SIP-only bootstrap is the only product path (ADR-0005)
- Headset vendors behind adapters; hardware events→application commands
- Refactoring: no feature loss; list feature/event/adapter impacts first
- Errors: never swallow; `catch (error: unknown)` + log in critical flows
- Completion: feature works, boundaries preserved, registry+tests updated, critical logs present

## File size (split if exceeded)

component 150 | hook 200 | file 300 | function 30 lines

## Backlog (no scope creep)

- **Transfer R6 BACKLOG**: `docs/softphone/real-integration/TRANSFER-REAL-ADAPTER-BACKLOG.md` — resume only when user cites it
- Do not block SIP/headset/settings on transfer gaps
- Do not remove transfer code without ADR
